{%- comment -%}
  Cashback confirmation — "your 7% is tracking", on the cart and the drawer.

  Usage: {% render 'cashback-offer' %}

  Shown only to a shopper the partner sent. The gate is CSS against the
  `cb-on` class that cashback-attribution puts on <html>, not Liquid: the
  server has no idea which visit this is, and the markup is inert to
  everyone else.

  ── Why it is not a site-wide banner ─────────────────────────────────────

  Because we would be buying our own traffic. A shopper who arrived from
  search, from an ad we already paid for, or from the WhatsApp number on the
  bag, and who is told here that there is cashback to be had, will leave,
  find the partner, click back in and cost us the commission on an order we
  already had. Cashback is a channel, and a channel is advertised on the
  channel.

  ── Why it says "tracking" and not a figure in dirhams ───────────────────

  Because we do not pay it and cannot promise it. The partner decides what
  clears, when it clears, and what a return does to it — all of which lives
  in their terms, linked rather than restated so it cannot go stale here.
  Naming an amount the shopper might not receive turns their complaint into
  our support ticket.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign cb_pct = settings.cashback_percent | default: '' | strip
  assign cb_name = settings.cashback_partner | default: '' | strip

  assign cb_show = false
  if settings.cashback_enabled and cb_pct != blank and cb_name != blank
    assign cb_show = true
  endif
-%}

{%- if cb_show -%}
  <div class="cb-row" data-cashback-row>
    <span class="mi" aria-hidden="true">savings</span>
    <span>
      <b>{{ cb_pct }}% cashback</b> on this order is tracking through {{ cb_name }} — it is paid into your {{ cb_name }} account after delivery.
      {%- if settings.cashback_terms_url != blank %}
        <a href="{{ settings.cashback_terms_url }}" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">{{ cb_name }}&rsquo;s terms</a>.
      {%- endif -%}
    </span>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
